                <pb facs="1404" n="1246" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1246"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Riddle to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23. Roumanian Series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 14, of March 1 last,
                    relating to Greco-Roumanian relations, I have the honor to inform you that
                    diplomatic relations between the two countries were last week officially broken
                    off. They have been practically suspended since September, 1905, as the
                    Roumanian representatives in Greece and the Greek representatives in Roumania
                    have been absent from their posts since that date. The Greek Government found
                    such an arrangement unsatisfactory, as there was no one to look after Greek
                    interests in Roumania, and accordingly declared diplomatic relations broken off,
                    at the same time intrusting the protection of Greek subjects and Greek interests
                    in Roumania to the Russian legation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. W. Riddle.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
